    <string name="help_intro">A native Android console for TheoTown, with a screen for every task.</string>
    <string name="help_section_start">Getting started</string>
    <string name="help_start_body">1. Sign in with the forum account. 2. Read the balance on Home. 3. Top up on the Top up tab, review the summary, then swipe to write. 4. Read or sync feature purchases after the write.</string>
    <string name="help_section_topup">Top-up</string>
    <string name="help_topup_body">The normalized expected balance is max(earned, spend) + amount - spend. The write is rejected above 2,147,483,647 or when the balance has no room under 100,000. A swipe-to-confirm control performs the write; the balance is read again and the two feature rows are checked in a short watch window.</string>
    <string name="help_section_features">Feature purchases</string>
    <string name="help_features_body">Sync reads first, writes only missing rows, and keeps a 12-hour stamp per account. If the rows stay missing it refreshes the session once, falls back to max purchase, and probes with a temporary row. The full watch can take more than a minute; use Stop to cancel.</string>
    <string name="help_section_security">Security</string>
    <string name="help_security_body">The password is sealed with RSA PKCS#1 v1.5 after an MD5 mask. Session data stays in memory. The app stores only the optional username and per-account purchase write stamps. There is no storage or notification permission.</string>
    <string name="help_section_build">Build</string>
    <string name="help_build_body">Builds, lint, and unit tests run in GitHub Actions. The APK is downloaded from the Actions artifact; there is no local Gradle wrapper. The release build shrinks resources and falls back to debug signing when secrets are absent.</string>

